{"id": "DelSFkMRRzq", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Shiva keep GANGA in his hair? 🌊 She fell from heaven hard enough to break the earth, and only Shiva could catch her.\n\nIt began with King Sagara's 60,000 sons. Hunting their father's stolen horse, they dug down to the underworld, found it\nbeside the sage Kapila, and called him a thief. One sound from Kapila, and they were ash. Only Ganga, the river of\nheaven, could free their souls.\n\nKings prayed and failed, until Bhagiratha prayed for thousands of years and Brahma said yes. But the earth could not\nbear her fall. So Bhagiratha stood on ONE TOE for a year, praying to Shiva.\n\nProud Ganga meant to sweep Shiva into the underworld. He caught her in his jata, and she was lost in it for years. He\nlet out seven streams, and one followed Bhagiratha's chariot (Bhagirathi). The sage Jahnu drank her whole for flooding\nhis yagna, then let her out through his ear (Jahnavi). She reached the ashes, and 60,000 souls rose to heaven. That's\nwhy Shiva is GANGADHARA. 🙏\n\n(Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda 38–44)\n\nWhere did YOU take your first dip in Ganga? Comment your ghat 👇 Save this, and share it with someone you went with.\n\nMore stories of Shiva and the gods: follow @therishikatha · rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n#ganga #gangadhara #mahadev #shiva #harharmahadev #harhargange #bhagiratha #gangaavtaran #ramayana #hindumythology #sanatandharma #mythologystories #indianmythology #varanasi #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792212496, "like_count": 8401, "comment_count": 41, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1132100869774098a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 63.101, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNmF8HPyCmBd8JQ30A9xPk3zJAZMHp7wxDmVx